# Release validation

When building, packaging or publishing a release, follow
`docs/RELEASING.md` and record evidence for each shipped target.

- Test the final extracted binaries after compiler, PGO and packaging changes.
- Linux/Steam Deck assets require cold and warm packaged-game startup and a
  short gameplay run through the supported Proton/UMU + DXVK stack.
- Exercise the target shader compiler, including prepared MSAA variants when
  AA is off. Run `WorldRendererTests.exe --screen-fog-compiler-only` as preflight.
- Windows tests, WARP, AppImage help and checksum checks are separate coverage.
- Shader/startup failures or unavailable required runtime tests block that
  target's publication; report missing coverage instead of claiming a pass.
- Keep precise runtime/GPU/settings identities, logs, images and hashes.
- Verify fresh installation and the previous release's update path.
- Require physical Deck evidence for claims of Deck hardware compatibility.
- Preserve user data, old artifacts and recovery evidence. Follow the existing
  Windows reparse-point safeguard before any worktree cleanup.
